 "text": "3\n\u0007A student tests two substances: solid K and solid L.\nTests on solid K\n\u0007The student dissolves solid K in water to form solution K. The student divides solution K into four\nportions.\n\u0007Table 3.1 shows the tests and the student’s observations for solution K.\ntests\nobservations\ntest 1\nTo the first portion of solution K, add a few\nwhite precipitate\ndrops of aqueous ammonia.\ntest 2\nTo the second portion of solution K, add a\npale purple solution\nfew drops of acidified aqueous potassium\nmanganate(VII).\ntest 3\nTo the third portion of solution K, add 1 cm3\ncream precipitate\nof dilute nitric acid followed by a few drops of\naqueous silver nitrate.\ntest 4\nTo the fourth portion of solution K, add aqueous\nthe solution becomes orange\nchlorine.",
